( x11vnc Service - Installation Guide) Tj
T*
( Share the currently logged-in X11 desktop on a Dell PC running Debian-based Raspberry Pi Desktop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Overview) Tj
T*
( The install-x11vnc.sh script installs x11vnc and xauth, configures a VNC password, and creates a systemd) Tj
T*
( service named x11vnc-follow-session.service. The service starts at boot and waits for the active local X11) Tj
T*
( user session.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Unlike a virtual VNC desktop, this displays the same physical desktop that the logged-in user sees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Requirements) Tj
T*
( Debian-based Raspberry Pi Desktop on a Dell/PC; an X11 graphical session; sudo/root permissions; network) Tj
T*
( access for installing packages. It does not require Raspberry Pi hardware.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 1. Install) Tj
T*
( Recommended - SSH tunnel mode: Only listens on 127.0.0.1 by default.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    sudo bash install-x11vnc.sh) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Optional - direct local network mode: Listens on TCP port 5900 on network interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    sudo bash install-x11vnc.sh --lan) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( On the first run, you will be asked to set a VNC password. Traditional VNC authentication uses only the first 8) Tj
T*
( characters. Re-running the installer keeps the existing password unless you reset it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 2. Connect to the desktop) Tj
T*
( Default secure mode: An SSH server must also be running on the Dell. On the remote computer, open a tunnel,) Tj
T*
( then point your VNC viewer at 127.0.0.1:5900.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    ssh -L 5900:127.0.0.1:5900 USER@DELL_IP) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( LAN mode: Find the Dell IP with hostname -I, then connect the viewer to DELL_IP:5900.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Important: A user must be logged in to an active X11 desktop. The service will wait when no qualifying X11) Tj
T*
(   desktop is active; it does not share the login screen.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(x11vnc | Debian / Raspberry Pi Desktop on Dell PC                                                                  1/2) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
