35 752 Td
( Operations & Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
( Useful commands and behavior for the installed systemd service.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 3. Manage the service) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    sudo systemctl status x11vnc-follow-session) Tj
T*
(    sudo systemctl restart x11vnc-follow-session) Tj
T*
(    sudo systemctl stop x11vnc-follow-session) Tj
T*
(    sudo systemctl enable --now x11vnc-follow-session) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Follow live diagnostic logs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    sudo journalctl -u x11vnc-follow-session -f) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 4. How active-session detection works) Tj
T*
( The helper checks loginctl about every 3 seconds and selects a local, active, user-class X11 session on) Tj
T*
( seat0. It identifies the X display and Xauthority credentials, starts x11vnc against that display, and restarts) Tj
T*
( x11vnc when the qualifying session changes. If no session qualifies, it waits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 5. Files installed) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  /etc/systemd/system/x11vnc-follow-session.service                    Systemd unit \(starts at boot\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  /usr/local/sbin/x11vnc-follow-session                                Session-aware launcher.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  /etc/default/x11vnc-follow-session                                   Binding mode: local or lan.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  /etc/x11vnc.pass                                                     Password file \(root-only permissions\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 6. Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
( VNC not connecting? Check that the GUI uses X11, that somebody is logged in locally, and that the service) Tj
T*
( logs show an active session:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE) Tj
T*
(    loginctl list-sessions) Tj
T*
(    sudo journalctl -u x11vnc-follow-session -n 40 --no-pager) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( If the first command reports wayland, choose an X11 session; x11vnc cannot share a native Wayland session. If) Tj
T*
( the service detects a session but cannot display it, inspect the logs for X display or Xauthority errors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 7. Security and configuration) Tj
T*
( By default, port 5900 is bound to localhost. To change modes, edit /etc/default/x11vnc-follow-session and) Tj
T*
( set X11VNC_BIND=local or X11VNC_BIND=lan, then restart the service.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Security: Direct VNC traffic is not encrypted. Prefer the SSH tunnel; if using LAN mode, restrict port 5900 with a) Tj
T*
(   firewall and never expose it directly to the public internet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(x11vnc | Debian / Raspberry Pi Desktop on Dell PC                                                                       2/2) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
